h", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Amy Klobuchar enters the final stretch of the open-seat race to succeed Tim Walz with a clear advantage. Every independent poll since September has shown her ahead by seven to ten points, and prediction markets price her win probability in the mid-nineties. She has raised roughly $7 million to Lisa Demuth's $361,000, giving her a dominant advertising position in a state that leans three points Democratic.\n\nRaters split between Likely D and Solid D, with none placing the race in play. Demuth, the state House Republican leader, has kept the contest visible through debates over crime, ICE operations, and state spending, and one Republican-affiliated September poll showed a two-point race. Still, the weight of polling, money, and expert ratings points to a comfortable, if not landslide, Democratic hold on the governorship.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9491, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9656, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9536, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9456, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9461, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9453, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9445, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9598, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.927, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.949, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "20